00:36:58,542 --> 00:37:09,480
So, in a way, I think one of the areas that AI has made the biggest impact would be computer science and now math. And it looks like science is a little bit different.

294
00:37:10,126 --> 00:37:18,460
I think the existence of wetlaps is very different because math and computer science always happens inside the computer.

295
00:37:19,120 --> 00:37:25,604
So I think that's one thing and another thing is I don't know if AI is able to extrapolate.

296
00:37:25,880 --> 00:37:31,400
Like if you think about discoveries, invention, asking questions that no one really thought about.

297
00:37:31,780 --> 00:37:38,084
I don't know if AI is able to just extrapolate and come with new materials for example.

298
00:37:38,414 --> 00:37:39,364
What do you think about this?

299
00:37:40,840 --> 00:37:43,160
I also kind of agree with that point.

300
00:37:43,580 --> 00:37:59,080
I mean, I see, AI is really good at interpreting what our knowledge we already know, but I'm always suspicious about whether AI can actually extrapolate our the boundary outside of the boundaries, our knowledge.

301
00:37:59,080 --> 00:38:04,300
because whenever I ask AI, just naive, question, "What, do you be?

302
00:38:04,300 --> 00:38:06,940
do you have any good ideas to improve something?

303
00:38:07,560 --> 00:38:12,220
And usually, the idea is, it's good, but not excellent.

304
00:38:12,740 --> 00:38:17,340
It's not like a totally new or groundbreaking idea.

305
00:38:17,460 --> 00:38:23,200
It's more like, okay, this is reasonable, but it sounds like someone already tried or someone already tried.

306
00:38:23,480 --> 00:38:25,420
Just modifications of that idea.

307
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:41,800
So I think for the science, it's really what the important thing is the extrapolation and science often comes from the surprising findings that are unexpected ones.

308
00:38:42,446 --> 00:38:48,360
So I actually have a little bit of the suspicion whether AI actually can have that direction.

309
00:38:50,670 --> 00:38:51,396
Do you have a say in this?

310
00:38:52,270 --> 00:39:01,120
Yeah, I generally agree, but also with the advancement of AI, nowadays the AIs can do more reasoning.

311
00:39:01,940 --> 00:39:19,960
So in the future, it may be possible that, given some first principles, you find some relevant information and then try to synthesize based on the principle, instead of just saying something.

