00:40:38,286 --> 00:40:48,260
Yeah, I mean, I think one of the things with AI I find really the most compelling and interesting is the how difficult it is to predict what it is it's actually going to do, right?

322
00:40:48,270 --> 00:41:04,040
Because normally, we have new ideas, new inventions come along in science, and we kind of understand them quickly, and we can project where it's going, but AI is evolving in real time, which makes it really hard to understand where this is going and the pace at which it's going at.

323
00:41:04,560 --> 00:41:10,240
In chemistry, we always say that a chemical reaction is impossible until it's not.

324
00:41:10,940 --> 00:41:18,532
And that means that people will say, you can never do this, and then someone will do it, And then people will know forever, you can do this.

325
00:41:19,022 --> 00:41:25,140
I feel like with AI, we're kind of in this same situation where people are thinking, I'm the same way.

326
00:41:25,262 --> 00:41:29,200
I think, well, we'll never be able to do this and we'll never do that, but then it will happen.

327
00:41:29,934 --> 00:41:35,460
And I think betting against AI is a really tricky thing because you don't want to be in the wrong side of history.

328
00:41:36,270 --> 00:41:45,200
